       "text": "I haven't entered this order, and I won't enter it as written. A 50 mg daily dose of amlodipine is five times the labeled maximum, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. You also haven't given a clinical reason, and the risk of serious harm is high. That risk includes profound hypotension, shock, and pulmonary edema, and the effects can last a long time because amlodipine has a half-life of 30 to 50 hours.\n\nHere are some options:\n\n- **Enter 10 mg once daily.** This is the maximum dose, and I can enter it now. If the patient needs more blood pressure control, you can add a second agent such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide.\n- **Discuss it with pharmacy.** If you think this patient needs an unusual dose, a pharmacist or the attending can review it first. The order can then go in with documented approval.\n- **Check for a typo.** If you meant 5 mg, or 10 mg, tell me and I'll enter it.\n\nWhich would you like?"
